  Figures exported to: C:/Users/marvi/Dropbox/Book/2nd Edition/Chapter 10/Output/graphs
  Data files: results.csv  results_lasso.csv  results_combined.csv

  PRE-TREND EVIDENCE
  Pre-2018 trend interaction = -0.0076 per year (p = 0.0005)
  Parallel trends is rejected: Georgia was already diverging
  from the comparison states before consolidation.

  ESTIMATES THAT IMPOSE PARALLEL TRENDS
  TWFE (baseline): DiD = -0.0427 (SE = 0.0183, p = 0.034)
  LASSO-DiD: -0.0213 (p = 0.182) -- LASSO dropped 1 of 4 controls
  (retained: lntotsup, lnfinaid, lnfte). Stata's lassopack rlasso retains all four,
  so there the LASSO estimate is identical to TWFE (see Section 10.11.5).
  Specifications that reach significance all impose this assumption.

  ESTIMATES THAT RELAX PARALLEL TRENDS
  SCM post-treatment gap   =  0.0307
  SDID ATT                 =  0.0338
  CS-DiD ATT               = -0.0042
  TWFE + state trends      =  0.0170  (p = 0.1933)
  All small and not significant, with differing signs --
  the pattern expected if the true effect is near zero.

  POWER
  Permutation p = 0.467 (one treated state, 15 comparison states: low power).
  LOO range [-0.0520, -0.0338] -- stable, but dropping a state does not relax parallel trends.
  Placebo (2012): p = 0.144 -- tests for a break at one date, not a gradual pre-trend.

  CONCLUSION
  These data cannot detect an effect of consolidation on
  operating expenditures. See Section 10.9.1.
